<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>considerObject2Covariance</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Whether to use the Object 2 covariance when Object 1 has no position uncertainty. If false, only the Object 1 covariance is used. Defaults to true. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>considerWorstCaseWhenBothCovariancesArePresent</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Whether to use the worst case (i.e. the covariance yielding the highest probability of collision) when both covariances are present and the Object 2 covariance can be considered. Defaults to true. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>aRelativeSpeedThreshold</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>A relative speed threshold below which the close approach is considered a low relative speed encounter and the algorithm is not applicable. Defaults to 100 m/s. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>aFrameSPtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>An inertial (or quasi-inertial) frame to use. Defaults to Frame::GCRF(). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>aProbabilityOfCollisionAlgorithmSPtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>A probability of collision algorithm used to compute the probability of collision from the critical (degenerate) combined covariance. If std::nullopt, Frisbee&apos;s closed-form solution is used (see note below). Defaults to <ref refid="classostk_1_1astrodynamics_1_1conjunction_1_1probabilityofcollisionalgorithm_1_1_alfano2005" kindref="compound">Alfano2005</ref>.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Frisbee&apos;s closed-form solution degrades when the combined hard-body radius is large compared to the smaller standard deviation of the critical combined covariance (sigma_min). In such cases, using a 2D probability of collision algorithm (e.g. <ref refid="classostk_1_1astrodynamics_1_1conjunction_1_1probabilityofcollisionalgorithm_1_1_alfano2005" kindref="compound">Alfano2005</ref>) is recommended. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
